# Chess knowledge pack - the chessboard (lesson 01)
#
# Teaches the AGI how the board is structured:
# 8x8 grid, ranks, files, colors, and starting zones.

# --- What chess is ---
chess is a board_game
chess is a two_player_game
chess is a strategy_game
chess is a turn_based_game
a_board_game is a game
a_strategy_game is a game

# --- The board itself ---
a_chessboard is_part_of chess
a_chessboard shows 64_squares
a_chessboard shows 8_ranks
a_chessboard shows 8_files
a_chessboard shows alternating_light_and_dark_squares
a_rank is_part_of a_chessboard
a_file is_part_of a_chessboard
a_square is_part_of a_chessboard

# Ranks are rows (1-8), files are columns (a-h)
rank_1 is a rank
rank_2 is a rank
rank_3 is a rank
rank_4 is a rank
rank_5 is a rank
rank_6 is a rank
rank_7 is a rank
rank_8 is a rank

file_a is a file
file_b is a file
file_c is a file
file_d is a file
file_e is a file
file_f is a file
file_g is a file
file_h is a file

# Starting zones
rank_1 shows white_starting_rank
rank_2 shows white_pawn_rank
rank_7 shows black_pawn_rank
rank_8 shows black_starting_rank

# Square colors
a_light_square is a square
a_dark_square is a square
a_chessboard shows 32_light_squares
a_chessboard shows 32_dark_squares

# How the board is oriented
a_chessboard shows white_plays_from_rank_1_and_2
a_chessboard shows black_plays_from_rank_7_and_8
